## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end event-driven thinking with basic data validation, simple transformation, and auditing on GCP. It combines Cloud Functions, Cloud Storage, BigQuery, and Pub/Sub with a focus on idempotency and minimal IAM.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven processing on object finalize
- Lightweight data validation and field normalization
- Idempotent writes via insertId and deterministic output paths
- Audit logging in BigQuery and error routing via Pub/Sub

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js Cloud Function skeleton for object finalize
exports.handleIngest = async (event, context) => {
  const bucket = event.bucket;
  const name = event.name;
  // read object from Storage, parse CSV, validate headers
  // for each row: validate, normalize currency, write to cleaned path
  // on success: insert audit row to BigQuery with insertId
  // on invalid: publish message to Pub/Sub and quarantine
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you implement idempotency for reprocessing the same file?
- What minimal IAM bindings would you apply for each service involved?

